{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Irreducible Polynomial.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Irreducible Polynomial.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"irreducible polynomial irreducible polynomial","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Irreducible Polynomial.md","fileName":"Irreducible Polynomial.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Irreducible Polynomial","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-13 19:45\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Polynomial Algorithms and Elimination]] · [[Polynomial Rings and Factorization]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Polynomial Algorithms and Elimination","Polynomial Rings and Factorization","Field","Unique Factorization of Polynomials","commutativealgebra.pdf","essentialsofmodernalgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Irreducible Polynomial.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Irreducible Polynomial.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"irreducible polynomial irreducible polynomial","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Irreducible Polynomial.md","fileName":"Irreducible Polynomial.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Irreducible Polynomial","heading":"Irreducible Polynomial","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"An irreducible polynomial is a nonconstant polynomial that cannot be factored into nonconstant polynomials of smaller degree over the chosen coefficient ring or field.\n\nOver a [[Field]], an irreducible polynomial that divides a product divides at least one factor. This prime-like behavior supports the [[Unique Factorization of Polynomials]]. Irreducibility always depends on the coefficient domain.\n\nThe source connects irreducibility to maximal principal ideals in K[x]. Quotienting by the ideal generated by an irreducible polynomial produces a field in which the coset of x acts as a root.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Polynomial A